From 97f9949c336ce11dda2d4dea25358005f12172d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:35:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/15] rdna-boosts: block 02: adaptive MTP draft depth

Sources: old 01 (whole block).

Amended r118 (PR #206, @briansp2020): with LLAMA_MTP_INGEST_TAIL set, a prompt ubatch that lies entirely
below the ingested tail no longer costs a target readback and a full synchronize.  The MTP hook returns
before its getters, and llama_get_embeddings_nextn[_ith]() call ctx->synchronize(), so the host used to
wait for both backends to drain after every prompt ubatch before it built the next one; the target also
copied that ubatch's nextn hidden state to the host (21 MB per 2048-row ubatch on Flash-Next) and waited
for it.  New staging API llama_set_embeddings_nextn_from(ctx, seq, pos) (default 0 = every row, so other
callers are unchanged) marks the rows that are never read: an ingested row p reads h(p - 1), and any
ubatch holding a row at pos >= ingest_from - 1 is never skipped.  Measured on a 31.5k-token prompt (2x
R9700, tail 4096): prefill 1488.6 -> 1509.8 t/s (+1.4 %, 95 % CI +0.9..+1.9), of which the hook half is
about +0.6 % and the readback half about +0.1 %; identical greedy text and identical draft counts (177
accepted / 364 generated), decode flat, prefill logits bit-identical, and no change at all with the
variable unset.  LLAMA_MTP_TAIL_READBACK=0 is the kill-switch (both halves).

Amended r125 (issue #216): the draft KV cache type now FOLLOWS the main -ctk / -ctv unless the
draft type was set explicitly (-ctkd / -ctvd / their env vars), instead of upstream's unconditional
f16 default.  The draft only proposes (the target verifies), so the greedy text is byte-identical
either way, while the draft context's KV shrinks with the main cache: on a dense 27B MTP run at
-c 131072 the draft's single attention layer held 512 MiB of f16 KV against 144 MiB at q4_0 -- 368
MiB a 16 GiB card cannot spare.  Decode is unchanged within noise -- the quantized draft cache just takes the native quantized-KV FA arm
(block 05): three alternating reps per arm gave 56.4-56.6 (f16) vs 56.4-56.5 t/s (q4_0) at -c 8192 -n 400,
and 80.8-80.9 vs 80.6-80.7 t/s at -c 102400 -n 3000 (protocol A scale), with ROCBLAS_USE_HIPBLASLT=0.  The
same-seed greedy text is identical across the two draft KV types and to --spec-type none on all four
protocol-A axes (R/P/C/K, -n 3000).  Issue #216.

Amended r153 (issue #234, @overdoingism): align the drafts of the sequences that verify in the same step.
llama_memory_hybrid::init_batch() splits a decode batch with llama_batch_allocr::split_equal(), which takes
one token per sequence set per round and STOPS when the shortest set runs out, so the longer sequence's
drafted tail becomes a SECOND ubatch and the target model runs a full extra pass for that one step.  The fixed
--spec-draft-n-max path never produced a length difference (every slot drafts n_max), which is why this
survived, but the adaptive controller holds a PER-SEQUENCE depth: two verifying slots routinely disagree and
one decode becomes two passes.  draft-mtp-adaptive now gives every drafting sequence the same cap for the call:
the deepest cap among them, bounded by the smallest HARD cap in the call (--spec-draft-n-max, the MTP layer cap
and the caller's per-slot n_max, which the server lowers as a response runs out of tokens) and by the expert
cache's verify band.  So no sequence is ever asked for more than it would draft when it runs alone; the only
case where a width shrinks is the smallest-hard-cap bound (a response nearing its end), which is transient and
keeps the pair in one ubatch.  Inert with a single drafting sequence, which is every llama-cli / MTP gate run.
Padding the shorter sequence instead is not an option: a padded row advances the recurrent state in
mem_recr->prepare().

Amended r154 (issue #234): the alignment stays INSIDE the drafter whose caps it changes.  r153 also shipped a
generic "cut the finished drafts to the shortest" in common_speculative_draft(); measured on the issue
reporter's own chain (--spec-type ngram-mod,draft-dflash with a DFlash2 draft, 27B, 2 GPU, recall + prose,
-n 200) that is a LOSS: the cut fires on every step whose n-gram match is shorter than the DFlash block,
truncates the OTHER slot's good draft, and the pair aggregates 65.6 -> 61.7 t/s (-6 %) while the prose slot's
acceptance falls 74 % -> 50 % (splits 12 -> 1, and the lost proposals cost far more than the removed pass).
The cut is right only for a mismatch a CAP caused, which align_draft_caps() handles inside the one drafter
whose caps those are, so it and common_speculative_impl::draft_truncated() are gone and a chain of different
drafters keeps its previous behaviour exactly (measured inert: 64.6 vs 64.4 t/s, identical draft counts).
scripts/gate-spec-align.sh grows a --spec-type ngram-mod,draft-dflash arm that fails if the knob is not inert
there, so this cannot ship again.

Measured (Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q4_K_XL, 2 GPU on the x8 root ports, -sm tensor --parallel 2 --kv-unified -c 32768,
greedy, n_predict 400, aggregate t/s of a concurrent high- and low-acceptance pair): 104.8-108.3 -> 140.1-140.6
(+30..34 %), per slot 72-74/57-60 -> 112/76; at 3 GPUs 86.5-87.0 -> 133.1-133.7 (+54 %); on the host-expert
shape (35B-A3B UD-Q4_K_M -ncmoe 40) 116.2-116.3 -> 147.7-149.0 (+28 %).  The decode steps that split read 58
before and 0 after at every one of those shapes (llama_memory_recurrent's RSPREP trace).  The equal-length arm
(two identical prompts) is unchanged (-0.4..-2.1 %), a fixed draft-mtp n3 pair measures 143.9 so the fix
reaches the equal-length checkpoint within 2 %, and a single drafting sequence is untouched by construction and
measured: the n_seq == 1 llama-cli text is byte-identical on/off, as is every single-slot server request.  The
two-slot pair's low-acceptance slot verifies at its neighbour's width, so the flag's two values are two numeric
CONFIGS -- exactly as --spec-draft-n-max 4 and 5 are -- and GREEDY-PURITY.md's promise is greedy text per
config, not equality between configs.  Measured so that this is not read as noise: every arm reproduces its
text character for character across runs (4/4 at 2 GPUs, 2/2 at 3 GPUs and on the host-expert arm), the on/off
divergence lands on the same character every time, and a fixed draft-mtp pair at depth 5 against depth 4 moves
the same slot the same way with no alignment in play.  The token rule is untouched: every emitted token is
still the target's own greedy sample at that position.  A multi-slot server upgraded across this change can
therefore produce different, equally valid text.  LLAMA_SPEC_ALIGN=0 is the kill switch.  Gate:
scripts/gate-spec-align.sh (2 and 3 GPUs, the host-expert arm and a mixed-drafter arm).  Issue #234.

Amended r185 (PR #169 re-assessment, @briansp2020's finding): bound the aligned depth by a VERIFY WIDTH where
there is no expert-cache arena.  r153's bound was the arena's band (`band / n_drafting - 1`), and r176 made
`band` answer only for a config with host-resident experts -- so on a band-0 config (all-in-VRAM, -sm layer, or
a model with no routed expert) a multi-slot draft was UNBOUNDED: four slots at --spec-draft-n-max 7 present
~28-32 rows, the batch leaves the decode kernels' small-batch families, and the DEFAULT recommended
speculator (`draft-mtp-adaptive`) runs 9.5-31.8 % slower than the same arm with the depth bounded at 16 rows.
The bound is now `verify width / n_drafting - 1`, where the width is the arena band when an arena is active
(unchanged) and LLAMA_SPEC_ALIGN_WIDTH_BAND (default 16, 0 = off) otherwise.  16 and not 8: at the two widths
the fixed-depth arms measure 16 rows AHEAD on 3 of 4 shapes (35B-A3B 3 GPU 432.7 vs 389.8 t/s, 2 GPU 387.2 vs
359.6, dense 27B 3 GPU 240.1 vs 211.2; qwen4exp Flash-Next GSQ-IQ3_XXS 2 GPU + resident PLE is the exception,
204.6 vs 220.8), so PR #169's "above ~8 rows each extra draft token costs more than it gains" does not hold --
the *unbounded* width was the defect, not width 8.  4 concurrent 300-token greedy requests, one binary, band
on vs off: 35B-A3B 3 GPU 330.8 -> 434.7 t/s (+31.4 %), qwen4exp IQ3_XXS 2 GPU + PLE 175.5 -> 208.9 (+19.0 %),
dense 27B 3 GPU 218.5 -> 249.6 (+14.2 %), and a fixed `draft-mtp` n_max 7 arm 310.9 -> 362.8 (+16.7 %).
3 slots also gains (+16.9 %); 1 and 2 slots are INERT (16 / 2 - 1 = 7 = the default n_max), and the 2-slot text
stays byte-identical, so it is a pure multi-slot change.  A host-expert config takes the arena band and is
untouched (same code path, verified in the log).  Gate: scripts/gate-spec-width-band.sh.
